WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:02.551
- Sometimes I can be so much of a fighter

00:00:02.551 --> 00:00:06.051
that, you know, I'm always ready to fight.

00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:08.547
That's the first thing.

00:00:08.547 --> 00:00:10.634
When you stop taking care of yourself

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.361
you get out of balance

00:00:12.361 --> 00:00:15.617
and you really forget how
to take care of others.

00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:17.593
Look, it was not one
thing Baltimore taught me.

00:00:17.593 --> 00:00:19.383
It definitely taught me how to hustle.

00:00:19.383 --> 00:00:22.109
I always say, you know,
worry about being respected.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:24.862
Never worry about being liked
because that's the trap.

00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:26.230
- She's an American actress, dancer,

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.950
singer, songwriter, and business woman.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.891
She launched her music career in 2002

00:00:30.891 --> 00:00:33.822
when she created the
metal band Wicked Wisdom

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:36.026
where she's a singer and songwriter.

00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:39.104
In 1997, she married actor Will Smith.

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:41.502
She's Jada Pinkett-Smith
and here's my take

00:00:41.502 --> 00:00:43.670
on her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.255
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:46.586
and I'm super curious to find out

00:00:46.586 --> 00:00:47.937
which one you guys like the best

00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:49.004
and as Jada's talking

00:00:49.004 --> 00:00:50.624
and if she says something
really meaningful

00:00:50.624 --> 00:00:52.168
or inspiring to you, make sure to leave it

00:00:52.168 --> 00:00:53.611
in the comments below in quotes

00:00:53.611 --> 00:00:56.222
so that other people can be inspired too.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.406
(whooshing)
(dramatic music)

00:00:59.406 --> 00:01:00.743
- I haven't had any regrets, you know.

00:01:00.743 --> 00:01:03.217
And it's sometimes really hard.

00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:05.259
I'll tell you a funny story.

00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:09.561
I remember right before
I got A Different World

00:01:09.561 --> 00:01:12.050
I auditioned for Blossom.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.493
- Oh!
- You remember the TV show,

00:01:13.493 --> 00:01:14.702
Blossom?
- Absolutely, yeah.

00:01:14.702 --> 00:01:16.672
- Do you remember her
friend, the young girl?

00:01:16.672 --> 00:01:17.739
- [Audience Member] Six?

00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:18.628
- Six!

00:01:18.628 --> 00:01:20.189
I auditioned for Six.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:23.054
Okay, I had my hair up
in a little ponytail,

00:01:23.054 --> 00:01:24.337
this little jumpsuit.

00:01:24.337 --> 00:01:26.125
I looked like I was about 12.

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:27.446
Got the role.

00:01:27.446 --> 00:01:30.133
Okay, got the role to play Six

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:33.883
and I was, like, I was
18, 19 years old then.

00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:37.858
I said, I looked at my
agent Nancy Rainford.

00:01:37.858 --> 00:01:40.637
I said Nancy, I can't do this.

00:01:40.637 --> 00:01:41.632
I just can't do it.

00:01:41.632 --> 00:01:46.432
I'm going to be miserable playing
a 12 year old on this show.

00:01:46.432 --> 00:01:47.765
I can't do this.

00:01:49.032 --> 00:01:51.090
We had to turn it down

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.840
and, let me tell you,

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.540
them folks were not happy.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.739
It was, like, who was
this girl think she is?

00:01:57.739 --> 00:01:59.339
You know, that whole thing.

00:01:59.339 --> 00:02:02.788
But within two weeks I
got A Different World

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:05.621
and that really taught me a lesson

00:02:07.016 --> 00:02:10.349
which was, you know, to really listen to

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.152
and follow my gut because
everything that shines isn't gold.

00:02:17.152 --> 00:02:18.468
You know what I mean?

00:02:18.468 --> 00:02:21.668
And so it really taught
me a very valuable lesson

00:02:21.668 --> 00:02:23.745
to just stay true to myself.

00:02:23.745 --> 00:02:25.291
If there's nothing that I haven't learned

00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:29.775
about this business, it's
really about staying true

00:02:29.775 --> 00:02:33.775
to why I'm here, why, you
know, I started acting

00:02:35.584 --> 00:02:38.912
in the first place and
what's important to me

00:02:38.912 --> 00:02:41.686
and keeping my artistic integrity

00:02:41.686 --> 00:02:45.968
as well as my creative,
my personal integrity.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.702
That was a big lesson for me

00:02:48.702 --> 00:02:50.112
and let me tell you,

00:02:50.112 --> 00:02:52.212
that was not an easy thing to turn down.

00:02:52.212 --> 00:02:53.703
You know, being a young actress,

00:02:53.703 --> 00:02:55.730
you got this opportunity for, you know,

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.062
this series regular.

00:02:58.062 --> 00:02:59.819
It's money (chuckles).

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:00.703
You know?

00:03:00.703 --> 00:03:02.343
But I just felt deep down inside,

00:03:02.343 --> 00:03:04.390
I was, like, something's coming your way.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.757
Just fall back.

00:03:05.757 --> 00:03:08.388
And then I got to meet,
you know, Debbie Allen.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.364
(audience applauses)

00:03:10.364 --> 00:03:13.650
Sometimes it's best to
just sit back and listen.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:17.730
I think sometimes I can
be so much of a fighter

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.230
that, you know, I'm always ready to fight.

00:03:22.124 --> 00:03:25.288
That's the first thing,
you know, like (yelps).

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:28.879
You know, and so I've
had to learn that, okay,

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:30.462
let me just listen.

00:03:32.343 --> 00:03:35.223
And so I'm just learning how to--

00:03:35.223 --> 00:03:37.519
The fight will never go anywhere.

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:39.558
That's always going to stay.

00:03:39.558 --> 00:03:40.955
You know, I've just had to learn

00:03:40.955 --> 00:03:43.081
how sometimes it's time to
put the gloves down, Jada,

00:03:43.081 --> 00:03:45.181
and just listen and
really be able to take in

00:03:45.181 --> 00:03:46.622
the communication.

00:03:46.622 --> 00:03:47.561
Just have it.

00:03:47.561 --> 00:03:49.696
Just have the experience,
have the communication,

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:53.220
just have it, just see what it can open.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.969
Just see, just see, just listen.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.451
Okay.

00:03:57.451 --> 00:03:58.837
Oh.

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:01.235
That makes sense (laughs).

00:04:01.235 --> 00:04:02.464
You know what I mean?

00:04:02.464 --> 00:04:05.397
But then there are times that I listen

00:04:05.397 --> 00:04:08.884
and I listen some more and I go that's not

00:04:08.884 --> 00:04:10.634
how this is going to go.

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:13.075
And then if there's a disagreement,

00:04:13.075 --> 00:04:15.584
well, then I have to fight.

00:04:15.584 --> 00:04:17.987
And then that's okay.

00:04:17.987 --> 00:04:19.881
Every day when I wake up in the morning

00:04:19.881 --> 00:04:23.464
I go into meditation
and I ask for guidance

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:28.298
from the powers, the intangible powers,

00:04:28.298 --> 00:04:29.798
and I get focused.

00:04:31.869 --> 00:04:33.860
I think about, what
does Willow need today?

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.138
Okay, let me check that off.

00:04:35.138 --> 00:04:36.169
Handle that.

00:04:36.169 --> 00:04:37.329
What does Jaden need today?

00:04:37.329 --> 00:04:38.716
What does Daddy need today?

00:04:38.716 --> 00:04:41.799
And okay Jada, before the day is done

00:04:42.662 --> 00:04:46.040
you better make sure that
you take care of yourself

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.496
and that's a new thing for me.

00:04:47.496 --> 00:04:50.449
When you and Jaden were first born,

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:53.131
I had forgotten how to take care of myself

00:04:53.131 --> 00:04:55.904
because you guys were my world.

00:04:55.904 --> 00:04:57.843
You guys were my everything.

00:04:57.843 --> 00:04:59.010
You still are.

00:05:00.614 --> 00:05:02.726
But I had forgotten how to do that

00:05:02.726 --> 00:05:04.400
and at the end of the day the one thing

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.271
that I always want to tell you, Willow,

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:07.764
and the reason why you always have

00:05:07.764 --> 00:05:11.287
to be in communication,
especially with me,

00:05:11.287 --> 00:05:13.673
your family, your
grandmother, your father,

00:05:13.673 --> 00:05:16.121
your brothers, your friends,

00:05:16.121 --> 00:05:17.599
the people who love you,

00:05:17.599 --> 00:05:20.891
you have to understand
that life is a journey.

00:05:20.891 --> 00:05:23.808
Communication creates partnerships.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:27.418
Okay?

00:05:27.418 --> 00:05:30.597
That we are here to assist you,

00:05:30.597 --> 00:05:33.597
that we can't make your life for you

00:05:35.382 --> 00:05:39.522
and we can't help you with
the things that we don't know

00:05:39.522 --> 00:05:42.522
and that you always have to remember

00:05:43.773 --> 00:05:46.940
to take care of you first and foremost

00:05:48.538 --> 00:05:51.748
because when you stop
taking care of yourself

00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:53.086
you get out of balance

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:56.108
and you really forget how
to take care of others.

00:05:56.108 --> 00:05:59.291
And I think that we've been taught that

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:02.003
taking care of yourself is a problem.

00:06:02.003 --> 00:06:04.888
And I'm a tell you something
about being a mother

00:06:04.888 --> 00:06:07.660
and some of the messaging
that we get in this country

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.795
about being a mother, that
you have to completely

00:06:09.795 --> 00:06:12.628
sacrifice everything.
- Everything.

00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:18.083
- You have to completely
sacrifice every single thing

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.509
and I think that what,
the re-messaging that we,

00:06:22.509 --> 00:06:25.543
as mothers, need to have and gravitate to

00:06:25.543 --> 00:06:29.442
is that you have to take care of yourself

00:06:29.442 --> 00:06:33.836
in order to have the
alignment and the power

00:06:33.836 --> 00:06:38.003
to take care of others at
the capacity that we do.

00:06:39.333 --> 00:06:41.343
Because it fills the well.

00:06:41.343 --> 00:06:45.176
What I believe that I
do takes so much energy,

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:50.187
so much work, from heart,
spirit, and creativity,

00:06:51.283 --> 00:06:55.450
that I have to be responsible
enough to take care of me,

00:06:57.023 --> 00:06:59.725
because you know what happens?

00:06:59.725 --> 00:07:01.320
Imbalance comes, and
you know what happens?

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.341
I look to you Willow

00:07:02.341 --> 00:07:04.188
and I say Willow, you've got to do this.

00:07:04.188 --> 00:07:07.021
Because if you don't, you become--

00:07:07.872 --> 00:07:09.223
(audience laughing)

00:07:09.223 --> 00:07:12.830
You become, I start looking towards you.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:17.132
I start making you
responsible for my happiness.

00:07:17.132 --> 00:07:18.554
And a lot of times you know what we do?

00:07:18.554 --> 00:07:19.748
We look to our men.

00:07:19.748 --> 00:07:21.861
We look to our husbands and our boyfriends

00:07:21.861 --> 00:07:25.310
and we go, you, I've
given all this up for you

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.853
and you've got to make this right by me

00:07:27.853 --> 00:07:30.485
and you're supposed to make me happy.

00:07:30.485 --> 00:07:34.554
Because we've lost our way on
how to make ourselves happy.

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:35.887
We lost our way.

00:07:37.647 --> 00:07:40.062
So what I had to do
and what I had to learn

00:07:40.062 --> 00:07:41.861
was how to get more balance.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.971
And over the years, each year, each day

00:07:43.971 --> 00:07:46.988
I get more and more and more
and more and more in balance,

00:07:46.988 --> 00:07:49.431
more and more in alignment,
and you know what?

00:07:49.431 --> 00:07:51.598
I get more and more happy.

00:07:53.221 --> 00:07:56.080
And the very thing that I
thought would make you unhappy

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.391
or make Jaden unhappy
or make Daddy unhappy

00:07:58.391 --> 00:08:01.837
actually is fulfilling
for you guys as well.

00:08:01.837 --> 00:08:04.857
Even though it might not
be a tangible reason.

00:08:04.857 --> 00:08:07.550
But the more happy I am and
the more fulfilled I am,

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.550
it works for the family.

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:13.878
And when I'm not, it doesn't.

00:08:13.878 --> 00:08:15.158
It's really that simple.

00:08:15.158 --> 00:08:16.901
You know, one of the things that I love,

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:20.080
one of the purposes of
why I became an artist

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.997
is to have the opportunity
to break boundaries.

00:08:26.701 --> 00:08:28.043
Right?
- Right.

00:08:28.043 --> 00:08:31.710
- It's one of the things
that I really enjoy

00:08:33.911 --> 00:08:37.911
being able to use art in
a way in which to break

00:08:40.057 --> 00:08:44.421
those boundaries and
break out of those boxes

00:08:44.421 --> 00:08:47.280
that we create for ourselves

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.485
and others create for us

00:08:49.485 --> 00:08:51.723
and I've always loved metal music

00:08:51.723 --> 00:08:56.025
and the only reason why
I didn't do metal music

00:08:56.025 --> 00:08:57.928
was because I'd always been told

00:08:57.928 --> 00:09:00.470
because I was black and
because I was female

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.087
that it was a genre that wasn't for me.

00:09:03.087 --> 00:09:05.790
And I just got sick of that.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.019
I was just, like, that's just not true.

00:09:08.019 --> 00:09:09.769
That's just not true.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:14.630
So I decided to go on
tour as a metal artist.

00:09:16.654 --> 00:09:20.721
One of the things I was
talking to Pete Berg

00:09:20.721 --> 00:09:23.906
and he called me and he
said, Jada, be fearless.

00:09:23.906 --> 00:09:25.721
Be fearless.

00:09:25.721 --> 00:09:28.554
And my husband said be relentless.

00:09:30.145 --> 00:09:32.868
So fearless and relentless, you know,

00:09:32.868 --> 00:09:36.220
are those two words that I
keep in the back of my mind

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.640
at all times when I'm sitting
in front of that monitor

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.527
and I'm like, do I have this?

00:09:40.527 --> 00:09:42.183
And I know we only have five more

00:09:42.183 --> 00:09:43.763
minutes before we have to--

00:09:43.763 --> 00:09:45.054
I don't have it.

00:09:45.054 --> 00:09:45.955
Do it again.

00:09:45.955 --> 00:09:46.918
Still don't have it.

00:09:46.918 --> 00:09:47.751
Do it again.

00:09:47.751 --> 00:09:48.918
20 hour shoot.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.525
We got to get it.

00:09:51.525 --> 00:09:53.157
(laughs)

00:09:53.157 --> 00:09:54.767
- [Interviewer] You got to be
the one that takes the hit.

00:09:54.767 --> 00:09:57.292
- I got to take the hit, you know.

00:09:57.292 --> 00:10:00.456
I got to take the hit
'cause at the end of the day

00:10:00.456 --> 00:10:01.878
nobody's looking at that screen going,

00:10:01.878 --> 00:10:05.500
oh man, you know, it took
her 20 hours to do that.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.775
They're going is either
they enjoyed the experience

00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:09.768
or they didn't.

00:10:09.768 --> 00:10:11.407
Nobody cares when the movie comes out,

00:10:11.407 --> 00:10:13.292
you know, all those bits and pieces.

00:10:13.292 --> 00:10:14.922
Make it good.

00:10:14.922 --> 00:10:17.437
Have what you want, you know.

00:10:17.437 --> 00:10:18.574
Have what you want.

00:10:18.574 --> 00:10:20.865
It is so painful to sit there

00:10:20.865 --> 00:10:24.615
and know that you didn't
get what you wanted.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:28.885
Then you sit there and you
watch that scene and go (sighs).

00:10:28.885 --> 00:10:30.358
It's unbearable.

00:10:30.358 --> 00:10:31.762
I've done it already.

00:10:31.762 --> 00:10:33.294
Not in this project, but ...

00:10:33.294 --> 00:10:34.163
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:10:34.163 --> 00:10:35.108
- You know, in other projects.

00:10:35.108 --> 00:10:38.430
It's a painful, painful, painful death.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:43.277
I think we as women have to
learn how to have acceptance

00:10:43.277 --> 00:10:45.932
for who we are and that takes time.

00:10:45.932 --> 00:10:48.080
You know, it's like as soon as I turned 40

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.769
I think that's when, like,

00:10:49.769 --> 00:10:52.756
real self acceptance,
like, like and adore me,

00:10:52.756 --> 00:10:54.001
like, boom, right?

00:10:54.001 --> 00:10:56.786
I've been working hard for me, you know,

00:10:56.786 --> 00:10:58.338
in my 20's through my 30's.

00:10:58.338 --> 00:11:01.121
Got to 40 and I was, like,
dag, I really understand

00:11:01.121 --> 00:11:03.058
what self acceptance means

00:11:03.058 --> 00:11:05.832
which then brings about
that self assurance

00:11:05.832 --> 00:11:08.639
and that sense of identity.

00:11:08.639 --> 00:11:10.581
You don't care what anybody thinks.

00:11:10.581 --> 00:11:13.334
You don't, you know, you
just playing your own game

00:11:13.334 --> 00:11:17.251
and I think that that's
really where that sense

00:11:18.845 --> 00:11:20.928
of self esteem comes from

00:11:21.801 --> 00:11:24.752
is just being okay in your own skin.

00:11:24.752 --> 00:11:26.862
And I think that I would
just tell young women

00:11:26.862 --> 00:11:30.903
to just stay on that
path of finding oneself

00:11:30.903 --> 00:11:33.854
because it doesn't just happen.

00:11:33.854 --> 00:11:35.289
It is a journey.

00:11:35.289 --> 00:11:38.299
And trying to be someone else

00:11:38.299 --> 00:11:42.068
might be someone's entryway
into becoming their own self,

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:45.872
but to know that, you know,
trying to be anyone else

00:11:45.872 --> 00:11:49.407
besides who you are isn't
going to get you there.

00:11:49.407 --> 00:11:50.240
You know?

00:11:51.545 --> 00:11:53.938
So as women we just have
to stay on that path

00:11:53.938 --> 00:11:56.410
of what I call that path of truth.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.493
Just finding what's true.

00:11:59.363 --> 00:12:02.363
And what's true for different women,

00:12:03.787 --> 00:12:05.921
you know, we all have different paths

00:12:05.921 --> 00:12:07.644
and different ideas of truth

00:12:07.644 --> 00:12:08.892
and as long as it's a truth

00:12:08.892 --> 00:12:11.594
that gets you settled into your own skin,

00:12:11.594 --> 00:12:13.336
well then that's the truth for you.

00:12:13.336 --> 00:12:15.582
- How'd you get an agent?

00:12:15.582 --> 00:12:16.711
- Let me tell you.

00:12:16.711 --> 00:12:19.467
(audience laughing)

00:12:19.467 --> 00:12:22.508
Talk about some name dropping, right?

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:24.938
So I had a friend that, at the time,

00:12:24.938 --> 00:12:27.503
was good friends with Keenen Ivory Wayans.

00:12:27.503 --> 00:12:32.323
And I got to meet Keenen and
we became very good friends.

00:12:32.323 --> 00:12:34.276
I ended up doing Low Down
Dirty Shame with Keenan.

00:12:34.276 --> 00:12:35.120
- Oh sure, yeah.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.517
- But I didn't have an agent.
- As Peaches, huh?

00:12:37.517 --> 00:12:38.350
- As Peaches, right.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:40.544
I didn't have an agent yet

00:12:40.544 --> 00:12:43.993
and I was, like, you know, how am I--

00:12:43.993 --> 00:12:46.426
I was just going through, you know,

00:12:46.426 --> 00:12:48.898
the list of agencies and I was like

00:12:48.898 --> 00:12:50.089
I got to get an agent.

00:12:50.089 --> 00:12:52.044
And so I literally called this one agent.

00:12:52.044 --> 00:12:54.127
Her name was Nancy Rainford.

00:12:54.127 --> 00:12:58.144
And I said I'm a really good
friend of Keenen Ivory Wayans

00:12:58.144 --> 00:13:00.613
and he told me to call you specifically.

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:03.310
(audience laughing)

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:06.144
She was, like, this
small agency on Melrose

00:13:06.144 --> 00:13:09.807
but, you know, she had
Michael Rapaport at the time.

00:13:09.807 --> 00:13:10.792
- Oh wow!
- Yeah.

00:13:10.792 --> 00:13:12.843
She had Michael Rapaport at the time

00:13:12.843 --> 00:13:14.642
so I say he told me to
call you specifically.

00:13:14.642 --> 00:13:16.964
You know, so I'm running this whole game.

00:13:16.964 --> 00:13:18.340
And she was, like, really?

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.631
She was like, why don't
you come in and see me?

00:13:20.631 --> 00:13:22.551
So I went in and see her, you know,

00:13:22.551 --> 00:13:25.554
and I put on the jazz hands, you know.

00:13:25.554 --> 00:13:27.422
(audience laughing)

00:13:27.422 --> 00:13:29.200
And she was like, you know what?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.515
I like you.

00:13:30.515 --> 00:13:31.866
I'm going to represent you.

00:13:31.866 --> 00:13:34.873
And I'm a tell you, she
was an awesome agent.

00:13:34.873 --> 00:13:36.468
She was an awesome agent

00:13:36.468 --> 00:13:38.231
and she had Michael Rapaport and I

00:13:38.231 --> 00:13:40.080
and she started my career.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.893
She started my career.

00:13:41.893 --> 00:13:43.813
And then she eventually
got out of the business,

00:13:43.813 --> 00:13:46.691
but she was the one that
started my whole career.

00:13:46.691 --> 00:13:48.151
- And it was that--
- And I got in the door

00:13:48.151 --> 00:13:49.502
because of Keenen's name.

00:13:49.502 --> 00:13:51.244
(audience laughing)

00:13:51.244 --> 00:13:52.275
- That attitude too.

00:13:52.275 --> 00:13:53.149
- That attitude.

00:13:53.149 --> 00:13:54.927
I was like, he told me you specifically.

00:13:54.927 --> 00:13:55.954
(audience laughing)

00:13:55.954 --> 00:13:56.823
- That's good.

00:13:56.823 --> 00:13:57.781
That's actually a--

00:13:57.781 --> 00:13:58.614
- Isn't that good?

00:13:58.614 --> 00:14:00.216
- That is actually
something that (laughs).

00:14:00.216 --> 00:14:02.566
(Jada laughs)
(audience applauses)

00:14:02.566 --> 00:14:03.597
That's great.

00:14:03.597 --> 00:14:04.978
I love that.
- I did, I did.

00:14:04.978 --> 00:14:07.112
Look, if it's not one
thing Baltimore taught me

00:14:07.112 --> 00:14:08.945
it definitely taught me how to hustle.

00:14:08.945 --> 00:14:10.525
(audience laughing)

00:14:10.525 --> 00:14:13.070
What I look for is the
power in all things.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:15.037
I look for the beauty in all things.

00:14:15.037 --> 00:14:17.064
And I think that part of the reason

00:14:17.064 --> 00:14:18.972
why I've been able to do the things

00:14:18.972 --> 00:14:21.014
I've been able to do is because of that.

00:14:21.014 --> 00:14:22.243
And I'm a tell you what,

00:14:22.243 --> 00:14:23.594
those streets of Baltimore

00:14:23.594 --> 00:14:24.747
gave me the training I needed

00:14:24.747 --> 00:14:26.904
to survive this game right here.

00:14:26.904 --> 00:14:27.861
It gone plan.

00:14:27.861 --> 00:14:29.425
You know what it is.

00:14:29.425 --> 00:14:31.737
You know what it is.

00:14:31.737 --> 00:14:33.606
I didn't go to college.

00:14:33.606 --> 00:14:34.495
- Right.

00:14:34.495 --> 00:14:36.699
- I learned on the streets.

00:14:36.699 --> 00:14:38.449
So it's all relative.

00:14:40.468 --> 00:14:41.748
You know, that's why it's very difficult

00:14:41.748 --> 00:14:44.416
to look at something and go
that's right, that's wrong,

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.294
because you don't know.

00:14:46.294 --> 00:14:48.319
You don't know where your gifts lie.

00:14:48.319 --> 00:14:49.870
You don't know where your treasures are.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:52.052
You just go with the flow
and make the best of it.

00:14:52.052 --> 00:14:54.928
- I always say, you know,
worry about being respected.

00:14:54.928 --> 00:14:57.370
Never worry about being liked
because that's the trap.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.254
That's where people manipulate you.

00:14:59.254 --> 00:15:01.465
And so my kids, you know,

00:15:01.465 --> 00:15:04.644
I did not teach my kids to be liked.

00:15:04.644 --> 00:15:07.610
I taught them to always
live by their truth

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.527
and to always respect others

00:15:09.527 --> 00:15:11.983
and to always reach to be respected.

00:15:11.983 --> 00:15:14.041
And, you know, different people

00:15:14.041 --> 00:15:15.488
will respect different things

00:15:15.488 --> 00:15:16.590
but at the end of the day,

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.261
my kids have the confidence

00:15:18.261 --> 00:15:19.587
to be who they are

00:15:19.587 --> 00:15:21.334
and that is all, as a parent,

00:15:21.334 --> 00:15:22.721
that Will and I can ask of them

00:15:22.721 --> 00:15:24.143
because that is where their power

00:15:24.143 --> 00:15:25.657
and their strength will come from.

00:15:25.657 --> 00:15:27.362
As parents you want to create, you know,

00:15:27.362 --> 00:15:29.353
boundaries that keep your children save

00:15:29.353 --> 00:15:31.773
but, at the same time,
create enough freedom

00:15:31.773 --> 00:15:34.333
that they can develop and
understand who they are.

00:15:34.333 --> 00:15:35.557
- My daddy once said to me,

00:15:35.557 --> 00:15:36.694
I think this is what he said.

00:15:36.694 --> 00:15:38.257
I love you too much to
deny you the privilege

00:15:38.257 --> 00:15:39.595
of making mistakes.

00:15:39.595 --> 00:15:40.555
- See, there you go!

00:15:40.555 --> 00:15:42.664
And that's what life is all about.

00:15:42.664 --> 00:15:45.192
I always tell my kids it's
not about not making mistakes.

00:15:45.192 --> 00:15:48.042
It's about how do you make them right?

00:15:48.042 --> 00:15:50.394
- That's right.
- Yeah.

00:15:50.394 --> 00:15:54.144
- It's the getting up
'cause we all make 'em!

